      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T21:26:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per an earlier discussion on a past CL, I believe VulkanDescriptorSets should be budgeted. My reasoning being that Skia owns the DescriptorSet resource (clients do not wrap this resource in their own object), we do not give clients a ref to it, and it lives within the resource cache - so it should count against our resource cache budget accordingly.\n\nObviously if we do not own a resource (as in it is wrapped, like wrapped textures), it should not count against our budget.\n\nBasically, IIUC, a resource should be budgeted if:\nA) it is owned by us,\nB) lives in the resource cache (either because it\u0027s not being used yet or it is but the resource is shareable),\nand C) does not give out a ref to the client (like for surfaces)\n\nListing out my rationale such that if my understanding is flawed it can be corrected for my knowledge! :)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "75019817847d7e4822953bceefaa63710d2e2864",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
